FILE HEAD:regress/gate_asan_sweep.sh
108: # that complaint and never entered main(); with it, 582 bytes of real emulator output
109: # ending in the abort diagnostic. Controls that the flag does not weaken detection:
110: # decstation/pmax still constructs (695 bytes, cpu:+memory:) and sgi/ip12 still reports
111: # its 4 sanitizer diagnostics.
112: #
113: # *** DO NOT TAKE "ASAN ACCEPTED THE FLAG" AS PROOF THE FLAG IS REAL. *** The discriminator
114: # this project uses for CLI effort tiers was tried here and FAILED to discriminate: this
115: # ASan silently ignores `no_such_asan_flag_xyz=0` and runs normally. The proof above is
116: # BEHAVIOURAL -- the flag changes what happens -- which is the only kind available.
117: export ASAN_OPTIONS=detect_leaks=0:abort_on_error=0:print_summary=1:verify_asan_link_order=0
118: export UBSAN_OPTIONS=print_stacktrace=0
119: 
120: # 15 machines abort here by design (see AB_EXEMPT). This host already has `ulimit -c 0`,
121: # but a host that does not would drop fifteen cores of a 93 MB ASan binary into $LOGDIR.
122: ulimit -c 0 2>/dev/null || true
123: 
124: #############################################################################
125: #  AB_EXEMPT -- THE KNOWN-DEAD SET, DATED AND NAMED.
126: #
127: #  Same idiom as gate_offline.sh's SM_EXEMPT/SC_EXEMPT, and for the same reason: a gate
128: #  that carries debt must carry it OUT LOUD. Entries are `type/subtype:YYYY-MM-DD`.
129: #
130: #  WHY A LIST AND NOT A FLOOR. A floor cannot express "none of them died" -- that was
131: #  B1's second half. A hard count could, but it is brittle: it breaks every time the
132: #  machine list changes, for no defect. A NAMED list is neither. Adding a machine that
133: #  works changes nothing; a machine that starts dying is red the same day; and a machine
134: #  that stops dying is ALSO red (see the "no longer die" check), so the list cannot rot
135: #  into a lie the way SM_COVERED did before it was cross-checked against real work.
136: #
137: #  WHY THESE FIFTEEN, AND WHY THE DIRECTIONAL FRAME DOES NOT COVER THEM.
138: #  All fifteen were MEASURED on both binaries: they abort IDENTICALLY under pristine
139: #  39748e3 and under HEAD (rc=134, SIGABRT, same reason text). So the directional rule --
140: #  the one at the top of this file -- classifies every one of them as "pre-existing,
155: #      which DISCARDS the lookup's return value, so a miss cannot be handled by the caller.
156: #      This is the printf-then-abort() that B1 could not see.
157: #    * `bus_pci_add(): pci_data == NULL!` -- devices/bus_pci.c:220-222, a machine adding
158: #      PCI devices to a bus it never created. Hit by mvmeppc/mvme1600.
159: #
160: #  *** THE DATE IS MINE, NOT THE OWNER'S, AND IT WANTS CONFIRMING. ***  gate_offline.md's
161: #  own lesson is that "a deadline nobody chose is a deadline nobody owns"; the owner has
162: #  previously chosen tighter dates than proposed. 2026-11-30 is a placeholder chosen
163: #  because these are whole machine ports rather than one-line fixes -- it is not a
164: #  judgement that they may wait that long.
165: #
166: #  hpcmips/{be-300,e-105,agenda} WERE here, and their removal is this ratchet's first
167: #  discharge -- exactly as the previous version of this comment predicted ("when that
168: #  lands, the 'no longer die' check goes RED and the fix is to DELETE those three lines").
169: #  #444 (a29f87b) fixed their constructor deaths, but the check stayed GREEN for a further
170: #  day because this gate's instrumented binary was built on 2026-07-29 -- the July binary
171: #  still died, so the exemptions still "held".  *** THE RED ARRIVED ONLY WHEN #450's round
172: #  REBUILT the binary from current HEAD. ***  A ratchet graded against a stale artefact
173: #  ratchets nothing; that is `asanstale`, measured live, and the second time in one day the
174: #  same staleness converted a real result into a wrong one.
175: AB_EXEMPT="
176:     alpha/3000/300:2026-11-30
177:     decstation/3maxplus:2026-11-30
178:     decstation/maxine:2026-11-30
179:     decstation/5400:2026-11-30
180:     decstation/5500:2026-11-30
181:     mvmeppc/mvme1600:2026-11-30
182:     mvmeppc/mvme2100:2026-11-30
183:     sgi/ip19:2026-11-30
184:     sgi/ip20:2026-11-30
185:     sgi/ip22:2026-11-30
186:     sgi/ip24:2026-11-30
187:     sgi/ip27:2026-11-30
188: "
189: 
190: #  A DELIBERATE COPY of gate_offline.sh's exempt_expired(). It belongs in lib.sh and this
191: #  round may not edit lib.sh, so the duplication is recorded rather than hidden -- see the
192: #  residual note at the end of this file. The behaviour it encodes was learned the hard
193: #  way there: an entry with NO date, an UNPADDED date, or a non-date never expired, and
194: #  still satisfied the coverage check. A malformed entry is RED and names itself.
195: ab_expired () {          # ab_expired <today> <entries...>
196:     local today="$1"; shift
197:     local out="" e d
198:     for e in "$@"; do
199:         case "$e" in
200:             *:*) ;;
201:             *) out="$out $e(NO-DATE)"; continue ;;
202:         esac
203:         d=${e##*:}
204:         case "$d" in
205:             [0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]) ;;
206:             *) out="$out ${e%%:*}(BAD-DATE:${d:-empty})"; continue ;;
207:         esac
208:         [ "$d" \< "$today" ] && out="$out ${e%%:*}"
209:     done
210:     printf '%s' "${out:-none}"
211: }
212: 
213: ab_is_exempt() {         # ab_is_exempt <type/subtype>
214:     local e
215:     for e in $AB_EXEMPT; do [ "${e%%:*}" = "$1" ] && return 0; done
216:     return 1
217: }
218: 
219: # Minimal file so machine construction proceeds past the loader.
220: printf '\x7fELF\x01\x02\x01\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x02\x00\x08\x00\x00\x00\x01' > "$DUMMY"
221: head -c 512 /dev/zero >> "$DUMMY"
222: 
223: #  stdbuf is what makes an aborting machine's reason text reach the log at all (B1). The
224: #  assertions do not depend on it -- they are exit-status based -- but the human-readable
225: #  half of this gate does, so its absence is a row rather than a silent downgrade.
226: check "stdbuf present (abort diagnostics survive the abort)" \
227:       "$(command -v stdbuf >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo yes || echo no)" "yes"
228: 
229: # Build the "type[ subtype]" work list from the emulator's own help text.
230: "$ASAN_HEAD" -H > "$LOGDIR/help.txt" 2>"$LOGDIR/help_err.txt"
231: 
232: #  firstalias(): the first SHELL-SAFE alias inside the LAST parenthesised group on the
233: #  line. Both halves of that sentence are load-bearing:
234: #    * LAST group, because a machine's *name* may itself contain quotes and parentheses --
235: #      `Generic "bare" ARM machine ("barearm")`, `ARM-based "Android" machines
236: #      ("android-arm")`, `DECstation 3100 (PMAX) ("pmax", "3100", "2100")`. Harvesting
237: #      every quoted token on the line would pick up `bare` and `Android`.
238: #    * SHELL-SAFE, because the alias becomes a word in an unquoted `for` list and a row
239: #      key. `silicon graphics` is the primary alias for SGI and is unusable as either;
240: #      `sgi` is the next one and is what the rest of this project calls it.
241: #  An unusable line emits X (type) or Y (subtype) and is asserted to zero below, so the
242: #  NEXT machine with a space in its primary alias is red rather than mis-attributed. A
243: #  failed type line also sets type="?" so its subtypes cannot silently inherit the
244: #  PREVIOUS type -- that inheritance is precisely how SGI's ten became rpi's ten.
245: awk '
246:   function firstalias(line,   p,i,seg,n,arr) {
247:       p = 0
248:       for (i = length(line); i >= 1; i--) if (substr(line,i,1) == "(") { p = i; break }
249:       if (p == 0) return ""
250:       seg = substr(line, p)
251:       n = split(seg, arr, "\"")
252:       for (i = 2; i <= n; i += 2)
253:           if (arr[i] ~ /^[A-Za-z0-9_.+\/-]+$/) return arr[i]
254:       return ""
255:   }
565: #  *** WHY THE EXISTING THREE-WAY CANNOT PIN THIS. ***  sanhit() already counts
566: #  `runtime error:` lines, so these shifts fed the HEAD column above -- but the gate's
567: #  assertion is DIRECTIONAL, and reverting the casts lands on dirty-upstream/dirty-HEAD,
568: #  which is scored "pre-existing, reported but not failed".  A revert is INVISIBLE to it.
569: #  These two rows are the pin.
570: #
571: #  Row 1 is BEHAVIOURAL: the five SGI subtypes that reach arcbios construction must
572: #  produce ZERO left-shift lines (and zero ASan, which re-pins #446 through the same
573: #  fresh binary).  It inherits gate 9's staleness caveat -- the binary is built from git
574: #  HEAD by build_asan.sh, and nothing yet asserts its age (tracked as `asanstale`).
575: #  MEASURED while building this round: a sweep against the stale binary reported the
576: #  PRE-fix counts with rc=0, exactly the void that caveat names.
577: #
578: #  Row 2 is a STATIC census, deliberately binary-independent so it stays load-bearing
579: #  even when the instrumented binary is stale: every `buf[3] << 24` in the file must be
580: #  cast (14 casts, 0 uncast).  It is also the ONLY row that can see the six sites no
581: #  current image drives with buf[3] >= 0x80 -- the sweep cannot witness those, which two
582: #  pass-1 seats named as the reason a UBSan-only oracle is not enough.  And it catches
583: #  the mutant the sweep cannot: `(buf[3]&0x7f)<<24` kills the UB, silently drops bit 31,
584: #  and passes every sanitizer -- but drops the cast count to 13.
585: #  KNOWN LOUD FALSE-POSITIVE: a comment quoting the uncast idiom reddens the census.
586: #  That is the safe direction; #446's NUL-byte lesson says never quote mutant syntax
587: #  verbatim in comments anyway.
588: #  *** THE LIVENESS TERM IS LOAD-BEARING, added after a pass-2 seat named the hole: ***
589: #  zero matching lines from a run that never CONSTRUCTED the machine is not a clean run,
590: #  it is an absent measurement -- a binary that dies at startup would have scored green.
591: #  Each subtype must show its own model line, so "never ran" reads RED, not clean.
592: UB450=0
593: for s in ip12 ip28 ip30 ip32 ip35; do
594:     timeout 60 "$ASAN_HEAD" -E sgi -e "$s" /dev/null > "$LOGDIR/ub450.txt" 2>&1
595:     sh450=$(grep -ac 'left shift of' "$LOGDIR/ub450.txt")
596:     as450=$(grep -ac 'ERROR: AddressSanitizer' "$LOGDIR/ub450.txt")
597:     live450=$(grep -ac 'model: SGI-' "$LOGDIR/ub450.txt")
598:     if [ "$sh450" != 0 ] || [ "$as450" != 0 ] || [ "$live450" = 0 ]; then
599:         UB450=$((UB450+1))
600:         note "#450 $s: shift=$sh450 asan=$as450 constructed=$live450 -- sites: $(grep -oE 'arcbios\.c:[0-9]+' "$LOGDIR/ub450.txt" | sort -u | tr '\n' ' ')"
601:     fi
602: done
603: check "arcbios shifts: five reaching SGI subtypes construct AND give ZERO ubsan+asan lines" "$UB450" "0"
604: 
605: #  *** THE FIRST VERSION OF THIS ROW WAS TWO GREPS AND A PASS-2 SEAT KILLED IT WITH ONE
606: #  TOKEN. ***  `(((uint32_t)buf[3]<<24) & 0x7fffffff)` keeps the cast SPELLING, passes
607: #  every sanitizer, and silently drops bit 31 -- both #450 rows stayed green over a real
608: #  value defect.  A pattern pins what its author thought of; the replacement freezes the
609: #  WHOLE statement (#444's S4 precedent) and exact-matches the multiset, so a mask insert,
610: #  a cast swap, a wrapper or a reorder reddens whether or not anyone predicted it.  The
611: #  probe strips comments and strings first, closing v1's loud false-positive too.
612: #  *** $HERE/../src, NOT $SEC: this gate never defines SEC, and the first committed
613: #  version of this line killed the WHOLE GATE at runtime with "SEC: unbound variable"
614: #  under set -u -- after the behavioural row had already printed ok, and with the wrapper
615: #  invocation still reporting rc=0.  A gate that dies between its rows and gate_end leaves

FILE HEAD:regress/gate_offline.sh
2230: #  the SUBJECT and demands a NAMED row notice, so it catches a fixture that has stopped
2231: #  reaching the code; the @@SELFCHECK@@ sentinel breaks nothing and feeds the detector's OWN
2232: #  comparator a deliberate mismatch, so it catches a comparator edited into always-passing --
2233: #  a state in which every row prints `ok`, and the row count, the identity row and the verdict
2234: #  token ALL SURVIVE, so the self-mutant and every other assertion here stay green.
2235: #
2236: #  WHY IT IS HERE AND NOT BESIDE ITS SIBLING: three of the four assertions read the
2237: #  FILESYSTEM and could live anywhere, but the fourth reads each differential's LOG, and six
2238: #  of the twelve do not run until after the selfmutant block.  $LOGDIR persists between runs,
2239: #  so asserting it there would grade the previous run's logs.
2240: #
2241: #  *** THE THIRD ASSERTION IS THE H, AND IT IS THE WHOLE POINT OF THE ROUND. ***  A name in
2242: #  SC_COVERED is a LEDGER ENTRY; sc_unbacked greps the differential's OWN SOURCE for a real
2243: #  @@SELFCHECK@@ block, so moving a stem from EXEMPT to COVERED and writing no sentinel is
2244: #  RED.  Without it this would be another G -- a check that a name appears in a list -- which
2245: #  is precisely the defect being corrected here.
2246: SC_COVERED="timer memory_rw footbridge m8820x m8invread diskimage_sync diskimage_parse diskimage_io diskimage_geom sh4_tmu rtc_range fbpending_bound"
2247: #  *** COVERED IS NOT UNIFORM, AND THE MANIFEST CANNOT SEE THE DIFFERENCE -- READ THIS BEFORE
2248: #  TREATING A GREEN ROW AS "the file is vouched for". ***  All but three of the COVERED stems
2249: #  route every row through one or two shared helpers, so the sentinel covers the file.  The
2250: #  count used to be spelled out here as "seven of the ten" and went stale the first time a
2251: #  stem was added; a proportion that has to be re-derived on every addition is a comment that
2252: #  will be wrong more often than right, so it is stated as an exception list instead.  The
2253: #  three that do NOT route through shared helpers:
2254: #    * sh4_tmu   -- 12 of 18 rows.  row1() is the only comparator in the file that takes an
2255: #                   expected value; row_three_timers/row_interrupt/row_interrupt_unie_clear/
2256: #                   row_stopped/row_no_freeze each hardcode their own, and cannot be probed.
2257: #    * geom      -- every row but the identity row, via BOTH geom() and parse(), which are
2258: #                   two separate comparators and are probed separately for that reason.
2259: #    * sync      -- both checks() and checkn(), for the same reason.
2260: #  rtc_range is in the UNIFORM group: every row goes through chk(), its single comparator.
2261: #  Named here rather than left to be re-derived, because the three-file exception list above
2262: #  is only trustworthy if additions are classified as they arrive.
2263: #  The per-file comments carry the scope; this is a LIVENESS control, never a census, and
2264: #  "going from 0 to 1 is not false comfort; calling 1 `the detector works` is".
2265: #
2266: #  THE EXEMPTIONS, DATED AND REASONED.  A FORTNIGHT, matching the deadline the owner chose
2267: #  over the Q4 one I proposed for the selfmutant list: 2 uncovered differentials, 1311 and 766
2268: #  lines, whose every row could be inert with this gate green.
2269: #
2270: #    ieee_store    HAS NO COMPARATOR TO SENTINEL.  No check(), no `rows`, no `failures`: each
2271: #                  section carries its own counter (abs_bad, rm_rn_bad, rm_rz_bad, rm_d_bad,
2272: #                  rm_vec_bad, interp_bad) with the comparison written inline dozens of times,
2273: #                  and this gate greps one summary line per counter for 0.  There is no single
2274: #                  point to feed a mismatch to.  A probe through a comparator NO REAL ROW USES
2275: #                  would prove nothing while reading exactly like coverage, so none was
2276: #                  written -- a forced control is worse than none.  Gate 3 does cover this file
2277: #                  against TOTAL comparator death, which is this control's own failure mode,
2278: #                  but by the vacuity-prone `grep -c PASS == 0` form its SM_EXEMPT comment
2279: #                  already flags, so it is a weaker cover than it looks.
2280: #    wdc_identify  NOTHING TO FEED A MISMATCH TO.  Read every row function: row_anchor,
2281: #                  row_slave, row_base_drive, row_identity, row_atapi_flags, row_wide_geometry,
2282: #                  row_no_lba_claim and row_selfconsistent are ZERO-ARGUMENT with the expected
2283: #                  value hardcoded in the body, and row(why, sectors) derives its expectation
2284: #                  FROM ITS INPUT (`got57 != sectors`), so changing the input changes the
2285: #                  answer too and no mismatch can be produced.  Injecting one means mutating
2286: #                  dev_wdc.c -- which is the OTHER control, already present.  This one needs
2287: #                  the nine row functions refactored onto a shared helper first: a round, not
2288: #                  a line.
2289: #  RE-DATED 2026-09-18 BY OWNER RULING, from 2026-09-02 -- a date that passed with no owner row: the
2290: #  "no exemption is past its dated deadline" row below went RED on every run from 2026-09-03, and the
2291: #  first run to OBSERVE it was 2026-09-18, the weekly battery having been disabled.  A re-date is not a
2292: #  discharge: both reasons above stand unchanged, and this list's SM twin was ruled the other way
2293: #  ("fix it, do not re-date", #537).  The comparison is a strict `<`, so these are valid ON 2026-09-27
2294: #  and RED from 2026-09-28.  Owner row: `scexempt` -- discharge, re-decide or delete before then.
2295: SC_EXEMPT="ieee_store:2026-09-27 wdc_identify:2026-09-27"
2296: 
2297: sc_missing=""
2298: for f in "$HERE"/diff_*.c; do
2299:     stem=$(basename "$f" .c); stem=${stem#diff_}
2300:     #  Match the STEM, not the whole token -- exemptions carry ":date" suffixes, and a
2301:     #  substring match would silently accept a stem that is merely a prefix of another.
2302:     _found=no
2303:     for _c in $SC_COVERED; do [ "$_c" = "$stem" ] && _found=yes; done
2304:     for _e in $SC_EXEMPT; do [ "${_e%%:*}" = "$stem" ] && _found=yes; done
2305:     [ "$_found" = yes ] || sc_missing="$sc_missing $stem"
2306: done
2307: check "SELFCHECK manifest: every differential is covered or dated-exempt" \
2308:       "${sc_missing:-none}" "none"
2309: 
2310: #  THE H.  Grep the SOURCE, not the ledger and not the log: a stem can only be COVERED if
2311: #  its own file contains the block.  @@SELFCHECK@@ rather than the summary text, because the
2312: #  token is what selfmutant.py filters and what the probe rows are named with, so a block
2313: #  gutted down to its printf still fails this.
2314: sc_unbacked=""
2315: for _stem in $SC_COVERED; do
2316:     grep -q '@@SELFCHECK@@' "$HERE/diff_$_stem.c" 2>/dev/null \
2317:         || sc_unbacked="$sc_unbacked $_stem"
2318: done
2319: check "SELFCHECK manifest: every COVERED stem has a real sentinel block" \
2320:       "${sc_unbacked:-none}" "none"
2321: 
2322: #  DATED ENTRIES, NOT A COUNT -- the selfmutant list learned this the hard way: `wc -w == 6`
2323: #  under a row named "shrinking not growing" made SHRINKING IT RED.  A count pins; a date
2324: #  expires, and shrinking is green by construction.
2325: #  The SM manifest's twin, and it carried the identical defect -- see exempt_expired() above.
2326: sc_expired=$(exempt_expired "$(date +%Y-%m-%d)" $SC_EXEMPT)
2327: check "SELFCHECK manifest: no exemption is past its dated deadline OR malformed" \
2328:       "$sc_expired" "none"
2329: 
2330: #  THE G -- and it is not made redundant by the H above.  The H proves the block EXISTS in the
2331: #  source; this proves it RAN, which is a different failure: a block behind a dead #ifdef, a
2332: #  differential whose compile failed, or a driver that died before reaching it all satisfy the
2333: #  H and fail this.  Assert the OK-token is PRESENT rather than "no FAIL line", because a
2334: #  detector that never started prints neither and a negative form is satisfied by a control
2335: #  that never ran.
2336: sc_notrun=""
2337: for _stem in $SC_COVERED; do
2338:     grep -q 'SELFCHECK the comparator can still fail' "$LOGDIR/diff_$_stem.log" 2>/dev/null \
2339:         || sc_notrun="$sc_notrun $_stem"
2340: done
2341: check "SELFCHECK manifest: every COVERED detector ran its sentinel" \
2342:       "${sc_notrun:-none}" "none"
2343: 
2344: # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #446 sgi_eaddr
2345: #  MOVED TO GATE 9 (gate_asan_sweep) AND DELIBERATELY NOT REPLACED HERE.
2346: #
2347: #  It was wired into this gate because the detector was pure SOURCE TEXT and so needed
2348: #  neither a binary nor a rig.  A pass-2 panel then built sixteen mutants against that
2349: #  detector and ALL SIXTEEN SCORED 7/7 -- including a two-character edit that restores
2350: #  the heap-buffer-overflow with no compiler warning, and a 217-byte file containing
2351: #  nothing but a C comment.  The replacement is a RUNTIME value oracle: it breaks on
2352: #  arcbios_init() in a real construction of five real subtypes and requires the ethernet
2353: #  string to BE the formatting of the MAC bytes passed beside it.
2354: #
2355: #  That needs build/gxemul and gdb, and THIS GATE RUNS NO EMULATOR AT ALL -- it is the
2356: #  offline differential of the linked float_emul.c, and it references the binary nowhere.
2357: #  Adding an emulator run here would have made the gate's own name untrue, which is the
2358: #  same defect as a check whose title does not match what it checks.  Gate 9 already
2359: #  constructs every machine and every subtype, so the probe went there.
2360: #
2361: #  Nothing is left behind here on purpose: a stub row asserting the probe merely EXISTS
2362: #  would be a row that cannot fail for the reason it names.
2363: 
2364: gate_end
2365: exit $?

FILE HEAD:regress/artifacts/ip30abortkill/ip30_abort_probe.py
1: #!/usr/bin/env python3
2: """ip30abortkill -- RUNG-3 REPRODUCTION ATTEMPT on unmodified `-E sgi -e ip30'.
3: 
4: TEST-FIRST: this exists BEFORE any edit, and it is run against the COMMITTED build.  It began
5: as a WITNESS attempt -- if it reproduces, it becomes the witness; if it cannot, the round
6: proceeds documented-only WITH THE ATTEMPT RECORDED, which is a different state from "did not
7: think to ask" and must not render the same.
8: 
9: *** IT REPRODUCED, AND IT IS NOW BOTH: the round's WITNESS **and** its SHIPPED DETECTOR.  The
10: sentence above said "not a shipped detector" long after two kill tables had made that false;
11: corrected 2026-09-18. ***  8/21 pre-fix -> 21/21 post-fix on one instrument, then 27 rows after
12: the pass-2 class closure.
13: 
14: ================================================================================
15: THE CONTRACT -- vacuity-floor clause (e).  A detector that says what it catches is
16: FALSIFIABLE; one that claims completeness is not.  Every CATCH below has a MEASURED
17: kill in regress/artifacts/ip30abortkill/killtable{,2}_20260917/.
18: ================================================================================
19: 
20: CATCHES:
21:   * reinstating any of the four abort() calls                (the pre-fix red, 13 rows)
22:   * deleting the announce at ANY of the SIX announce sites   (M3,M4,M7,M8 + the rd txt rows)
23:   * deleting either surviving store (0x10020, 0x10028)       (isr keep, isr clr / M1)
24:   * re-inserting the dropped 0x10030 clear-on-write          (isr drop 30 / M2)
25:   * moving the tick guard between bits 49 and 50             (tick 50 txt + tick 49 / M5)
26:   * mirroring d->isr into a DECLINED read, AT BOTH READ ARMS  (isr 20 rd val / M10,
27:                                                              isr 28 rd val / M11)
28:   * collapsing the two latch bits onto one, IN THE TICK->ISR DIRECTION ONLY
29:                                                              (xbit isr / M6)
30:   * defeating the latch mask outright AT THE 0x10020-READ SITE ONLY
31:                                                              (latch 1x / M9)
32: 
33: *** THOSE TWO LINES ONCE READ WITHOUT THEIR QUALIFIERS, AND THE opus5 F2 SEAT MEASURED BOTH
34: UNQUALIFIED CLAIMS FALSE -- EIGHT MUTANTS, ALL 27/27, SIX INSIDE CELLS THIS CONTRACT CALLED
35: CLOSED.  Corrected 2026-09-18 on the fable5 adjudication. ***
36: 
37: THE LATCH IS NOT A SHARED RESOURCE WITH TWO FAILURE MODES.  It is SIX DUPLICATED STATEMENTS,
38: one `d->warned |= IP30_W_*' beside every announce -- the same duplication the ANNOUNCE axis was
39: decomposed for.  The real space is {6 sites} x {announce fires, latch sets} = twelve cells, plus
40: {2 collision directions} = FOURTEEN.  THIS DETECTOR ROWS SIX OF THEM.
41: 
42:   * `latch 1x' visits 0x10020-RD then 0x10028-RD.  The FIRST access latches, so the SECOND
43:     arm's latch-set is never load-bearing: MF_nolatchset28rd deletes the latch set in an arm
44:     this row literally traverses and scores 27/27.
45:   * `xbit' runs TICK then ISR -- the OPPOSITE order from the hazard the product comment names
46:     ("a guest write to Set-ISR would silence the TIMER diagnostic forever").  Seeing that needs
47:     tick -> ISR -> tick.  MA_assign20wr and MD_assigntick are both 27/27.
48: 
49: MEASURED ESCAPES, ALL 27/27, ranked by what they admit (regress/artifacts/ip30abortkill/
50: opusF2_20260918/):
51:   ME_nolatchsettick  WORST -- one guest `sd' arming imask0 bit 50 gives AN ANNOUNCE PER TICK,
52:                      FOREVER: guest-drivable floodclass on the arm this round de-fatalised
53:   MA_assign20wr      `|=' -> `=' at 0x10020-WR: one character, falsifies the two-bit design
54:   MD_assigntick      the same at TICK, the other collision direction
55:   MB/MF/MG           delete the latch SET at 0x10020-WR / 0x10028-RD / 0x10030-WR: bounded
56:                      per-arm floods
57:   MH_nocounter       delete `d->reg_0x20000 += 1000': COVERAGE DEBT, not a floor cell -- the
58:                      counter is UNCONDITIONAL, above the de-fatalised guard, so it is
59:                      fix-independent (fable5 ruling)
60:   MC_len4            `&& len == 4' on the 0x10020 write guard: the WIDTH axis, disclosed below
61: 
62: *** THE CLOSURE IS OWED IN-ROUND, NOT FILED (fable5, 2026-09-18): six of the eight escapes
63: weaken statements THE FIX'S OWN DIFF INTRODUCED, which is the canonical clause-(d) shape, and
