HEAD:regress/wdc_addtoinbuf_probe.py
1: """wdcaddtoinbufbound -- RUNG-3 WITNESS.  Real guest instructions, real address
2: decode, real memory_rw, on an UNMODIFIED in-tree machine description
3: (`evbmips -e malta`).  No device is added and no machine description is edited.
4: 
5: THE DEFECT.  The guest WRITE arm of the wdc data port pushes bytes into the
6: shared inbuf ring with NO phase guard.  During an ATAPI DATA-IN transfer the
7: one diagnostic that could announce a stray write is suppressed, because its
8: condition requires !atapi_cmd_in_progress and that flag is 1 for the whole of
9: DATAIN.  Injected bytes grow `head` WITHOUT touching `atapi_len`, so they sit
10: in the ring ahead of the next chunk and the guest's whole next chunk arrives
11: SHIFTED.
12: 
13: THE ORACLE IS ABSOLUTE, NOT RELATIVE.  Chunk 2's bytes are poisoned at known
14: image offsets, so the fixed leg's expected values are tied to DISK CONTENT
15: through a channel outside the ring -- not merely "different from the shipped
16: leg".
17: 
18: THE PATH (all references GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_wdc.c at HEAD c125450):
19:   wd_command(7) <- 0xa0   wdc_command() ATAPI_PKT_CMD arm: sets
20:                           atapi_cmd_in_progress=1, atapi_phase=PHASE_CMDOUT.
21:   wd_data(0)   <- 12 CDB bytes (READ(10), LBA 0, 128 blocks -- see READ_BLOCKS
22:                           below for why 128 and not 32).  On the 12th,
23:                           inbuf_len==12 and the dispatch
24:                           fires (guarded by atapi_cmd_in_progress && !badlen_this
25:                           && atapi_phase==PHASE_CMDOUT && inbuf_len==12).
26:                           diskimage_scsicommand() READ(10) -> res==1,
27:                           data_in_len=65536; atapi_len clamped to 32768 and
28:                           32768 bytes pushed; atapi_phase=PHASE_DATAIN.
29:   wd_data(0)   -> 32767 byte reads.  Each pops one byte and decrements
30:                           atapi_len (consumed = len==4?4:(len>=2?2:1), clamped
31:                           to what remains).  atapi_len -> 1, ring holds 1.
32:   wd_data(0)   <- ONE 2-byte store.  The write arm's `case 2:` pushes
33:                           idata&0xff then (idata>>8)&0xff -- 0xa5 then 0x5a for
34:                           0x5aa5 little-endian.  atapi_len is UNTOUCHED.
35:   wd_data(0)   -> one byte read.  Pops the last chunk-1 byte, atapi_len -> 0,
36:                           and the re-arm fires: atapi_received(32768) <
37:                           data_in_len(65536), so atapi_len = 32768 and
38:                           data_in[32768+j] is pushed ONTO THE DIRTY RING.
39:   wd_data(0)   -> the next reads.  *** SHIPPED: the guest is handed its own
40:                           injected bytes back as disk data.  FIXED: chunk 2. ***
41: 
42: STATUS ORACLE, PINNED FROM SOURCE AND NOT FROM A MEASUREMENT.  status_byte()
43: ORs DRDY|DSC (0x50, diskimage_exist true), DRQ (0x08) when head != tail, DRQ
44: again when atapi_cmd_in_progress && (atapi_phase & WDCS_DRQ) -- PHASE_DATAIN is
45: WDCS_DRQ|WDCI_IN so that arm is set too -- and ERR (0x01) only when d->error.
46: wdc_command() assigns `d->error = 0` at its top, so after ATAPI_PKT_CMD the ERR
47: bit is CLEAR.  Expected: 0x58.  (The wdcringambig probe sees 0x59 because it
48: issues no command at all and the power-on d->error = 1 stands.)
49: 
50: WHY FREE-RUNNING AND NOT `step`:  DEVINIT sets d->data_debug = 1, so every
51: data-port access calls debug().  debug() adds 1 to `verbose` when single_step is
52: set and subtracts 1 when emul_executing, so a STEPPED run prints a line per
53: access while a FREE-RUNNING run at default verbosity has v == -1 and prints
54: nothing.  The probe therefore breakpoints and continues.
55: 
56: CONTROLS CARRIED (both mandated for an access witness):
57:   A  RAM LIVENESS      a known value round-trips through plain RAM using the
58:                        IDENTICAL sb/lbu instruction shapes.
59:   B  DEVICE SIGNATURE  two reads of the SAME data-port address return PUSH
60:                        ORDER (0x5a then 0xa5).  A memory cell cannot do this;
61:                        RAM would return a5,a5.
62:   D  DISK CONTENT      the first DATA-IN byte is the poisoned image byte 0xC0,
63:                        so the ring demonstrably holds real disk data.
64:   CONTROL 0            every hand-assembled word is checked against the
65:                        emulator's OWN disassembler.  A wrong register field
66:                        silently yields 0, which several rows would accept.
67: 
68: NOTHING IN THE REPO IS WRITTEN.  Both trees under measurement are copies under
69: /tmp, and the CD image is generated under /tmp.
70: CONTRACT -- vacuity-floor clause (e).
71: 
72:   WHY THIS EXISTS AT ALL, and it is not a preference: the shipped 128-row offline

HEAD:regress/ppc_rldicl_probe.py
490: #
491: #  The witness this file is derived from is a FAMILY instrument: it also rows
492: #  X(rldimi) and X(rlwimi), which carry their OWN measured defects (ppcrldimimask,
493: #  ppcrlwimiwidth) that #522 does not touch and must not touch.  Shipping those rows
494: #  in a DETECTOR would make it PERMANENTLY RED until two unrelated rounds land --
495: #  a detector that cannot be green is a different fault from the one it was written
496: #  to catch, and a gate row over it would have to be ignored, which is how a gate
497: #  stops being read at all.
498: #
499: #  So this detector is scoped to X(rldicl).  The three sibling rows stay in the
500: #  witness at regress/artifacts/ppcrldiclzero/, which is the EVIDENCE for those two
501: #  filed rows and is correctly red there.  When either is fixed, its rows move here
502: #  or into a detector of its own -- that is a decision for those rounds, not this one.
503: #
504: #  MEASURED: witness 19/27 committed and 24/27 fixed, the five flipped rows being
505: #  exactly the ones kept below.  **THIS FILE HAS 19 ROWS, NOT 24** -- an earlier draft
506: #  of this note carried the witness's own post-fix count straight across, which a
507: #  pass-2 seat caught.  It is 19/19 on the fix and 14/19 pre-fix
508: #  (killtable_20260910/SCORES.txt).
509: 
510: #  =============================== CONTRACT (clause (e)) =========================
511: #
512: #  WHAT THIS DETECTOR IS DESIGNED TO CATCH, and what it is NOT.  The boundary below
513: #  is MEASURED -- every entry was established by a mutant that was built and scored,
514: #  not by reasoning about the row set.
515: #
516: #  CAUGHT:  the mask variable; the mask bit positions; the mask end bound; `&' -> `|';
517: #           the mask ignored entirely; the `mb'-field decode INCLUDING its high bit;
518: #           rotate-versus-shift (the census sees SHL(all-ones,n) != all-ones); the
519: #           rotate AMOUNT at SH=0, 8, 32 and 63; the destination width; the `ra'-field
520: #           decode for ra >= 16; and the record form's CR0 result.
521: #
