15: `grep -A14 '^AB_EXEMPT="' regress/gate_asan_sweep.sh`), and its own comment calls that date a placeholder -- so the
16: round owes a decision on that table first (re-date per machine, or exempt the table with a reason: its twelve are
17: whole-machine ports).  Filed by the Fable 5.1 adjudication of `#550` (ruling 8, `S2`), which also widened the checker
18: header's sentence to say nothing enforces it.
