12:   line giving the reason for THAT date, in owed-work order: `ppc_rldicl_probe.py` 10-08 (the cheapest: 24/24 in under
13:   a second on a machine `gate_ppc.sh` already runs); `ip30_abort_probe.py` 10-15 (33/33 in 568 s -- a long gate
14:   guest); the four Alpha probes on four working days in a row, `alpha_tbi` 10-22, `lca_badval` 10-23, `lca_widewrite`
15:   10-26, `lca_isalane` 10-27 (one harness round giving an `-E alpha -e alphabook1` session a gate home discharges all
16:   four); and the four wdc two-leg differentials a week or more apart, `wdc_altoffset` 11-05, `wdc_altoffset_4bit`
17:   11-12, `wdc_altoffset_sig` 11-19, `wdc_addtoinbuf` 12-03, each owing its own instrument work (11-26 skipped).  The
18:   table's header records the dispersal and that NOTHING enforces distinct dates (filed, `exemptdistinct`).
